# decision Manifest-changing commands are transactions

`add`, `update`, `set`, and `wire` stage every manifest, lock, cache, surface, and ecosystem
edit before publishing any of them. A failure before commit leaves every tracked file byte-for-byte
unchanged; a commit failure rolls back already-published files. `wire` is idempotent and may repair
an intentionally partial dependency without changing its identity.

# decision Exit codes classify outcomes

Exit 0 means the requested state was reached (warnings may still be present). Exit 1 means a valid
request found drift, failed trust, a missing Refresh prerequisite, or another operational failure.
Exit 2 means invocation or resolution failed: invalid flags, absent input, unknown identity, or a
location from which no input could be read. Preserve these classes across subcommands.

# decision Output separates records from diagnostics

Machine-consumable records and command results go to stdout, one record per line unless the command
explicitly emits JSON or a document. Progress, warnings, summaries, and errors go to stderr. Durable
state belongs in the manifest, lock, or `.git-a2a/`; command delivery history is never invented.

# invariant Dry runs and checks do not mutate

`--dry-run`, `--check`, offline inspection, help, and validation paths do not change tracked files,
the lock, or `.git-a2a/`.

# decision Dependency status and roster refresh are distinct

The status table contains dependencies only; the consumer module is reported once in a footer,
with detailed diagnostics reserved for `-v`. An absent managed `AGENTS.md` block is `SYNC none`
and healthy, while an existing block that differs from the renderer is `stale`. After `sync` has
created a block, every dependency mutation re-renders that existing block as its final step and
never creates one implicitly. `--no-refresh` on add, update, set, pin, unpin, and wire skips the
package-manager Refresh phase without skipping deterministic manifest, lock, wiring, or roster
updates. Human status output expands its table with spaces through Go's tabwriter so every column
starts at the same position even when a source, ref, or wiring summary is longer than the header.

# decision Prerequisite reporting is shared with adapters

`doctor` always checks Git >= 2.25, warns below 2.27, and unions tools from detected ecosystem
markers with ecosystems explicitly named by wired dependencies. Human and JSON output include
version, PATH state, and the platform install hint; any required missing or incompatible tool is
exit 1. `status -v` exposes the same state. `add`, `wire`, `update`, and `set` preserve a completed
manifest edit and warn when only downstream Refresh is unavailable; a direct adapter `Refresh`
returns the shared actionable error.

# decision Fetch restores cache from immutable lock state

`git-a2a fetch [ID ...]` is the non-mutating durable-state repair command for `.git-a2a/cache`.
It fetches each manifest at the exact lock commit, validates the manifest SHA-256, stages the
cache, and atomically replaces only that dependency's cache. `--surface` also verifies the locked
tree id. It never resolves the manifest ref, rewrites manifest/lock, snapshots cards, or invokes
adapters; missing lock coordinates or hash mismatches exit 1 and preserve the old cache.

# decision Usage is a deterministic agent briefing

`git-a2a usage` prints at most 60 lines with exactly eight routine commands, one example each,
exit classes, structured-output guidance, and the canonical reference. `--prompt` appends the
complete fresh-agent workflow and `--json` returns the same ordered lines. Both forms are embedded
constants: they do not inspect the repository, network, terminal, clock, or environment.

# decision Authoring helpers construct valid manifests without prompts

`agent add/remove/list`, `export add`, and `policy set` are non-interactive, noun-first helpers
for manifest authors. Mutations load and validate the existing manifest, apply exactly the
requested typed change, validate again, emit canonical YAML atomically, and refresh an existing
AGENTS.md managed block. A roster-refresh failure restores the original manifest and roster.
Repeated `--scope` and `--contact` flags preserve declaration order; contact fields use
comma-separated `key=value` pairs and `|` only inside list values such as intents and labels.
They accept `--yes` as a no-op for automation. `init --example lib|app` writes a complete valid,
commented starting manifest and never overwrites an existing one.

# decision Explain embeds the generated normative field reference

`git-a2a explain PATH [--json]` reads no repository, environment, clock, or network. Its content
is the byte-identical generated `docs/manifest-reference.md` embedded at build time; the docs
generator updates and drift-checks both copies, so the command cannot become a second normative
source. Authors may omit `[]` from array paths (`agents.contacts.kind` resolves to
`agents[].contacts[].kind`). Unknown paths exit 2.
